From 6ee59f2f0234fcae57ca1e731c44f70cd92697ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HyperHLE iOS <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:10:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support the iOS arm64 JIT host

Changes needed to run dynarmic's arm64 backend inside an iOS app. Based
on Applesauce's "Support the iOS arm64 JIT host" (johnny901901901/dynarmic
f488f760), extended to pick the JIT memory strategy at runtime:

- oaknut CodeBlock: on iOS 26+ with a debugger attached, ask it for the
  region with `brk #0xf00d` (StikDebug's script) and write through a
  vm_remap alias; with CS_DEBUGGED (TrollStore "Enable JIT", AltJIT,
  StikDebug before iOS 26) use anonymous memory flipped between RW and
  RX with mprotect; otherwise use a MAP_JIT RWX region (the
  dynamic-codesigning entitlement), failing with bad_alloc rather than
  trapping when JIT is not enabled at all. The region is reused for the
  life of the process.
- address_space / a32_address_space: write through the writable view and
  release the debugger after the prelude is emitted.
- spin_lock_arm64: use the Apple-compatible sequence.
- block_range_information: replace boost::icl::interval_map with a plain
  std::map of discrete intervals. The interval_map instantiation does not
  build against the Boost version used for the iOS toolchain.
